---
import { url } from '../../url';
import Doc from '../../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { company, email, product } from '../../site';

const subject = encodeURIComponent('Delete my Wallyt account');
const body = encodeURIComponent(
  'Please delete my Wallyt account. I am sending this from the email address I sign in with.',
);
---

<Doc
  title="Delete your Wallyt account"
  eyebrow="Wallyt"
  eyebrowHref="/wallyt"
  meta={`Wallyt, by ${company.brand}`}
  product={product('wallyt')}
  description="How to delete your Wallyt account, what is deleted, and what stays with your groups."
>
  <p>
    You can delete your Wallyt account and the personal data that goes with it at any time, in the
    app or by asking us. You don’t need the app installed to ask.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open Wallyt on your phone or on the web, and sign in.</li>
    <li>Tap the person icon in the top right (Account), then <strong>Delete account</strong> at the bottom.</li>
    <li>
      Wallyt lists what will happen to each of your groups. Tap <strong>Continue</strong>, type your
      email address to confirm, and tap <strong>Delete account</strong>.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>Your account is deleted straight away, and you are signed out.</p>

  <h2>By email</h2>
  <div class="request">
    <a class="button primary" href={`mailto:${email}?subject=${subject}&body=${body}`}>
      Email a deletion request
    </a>
    <p>Opens your email app with the request written for you. Send it from the address you sign in with.</p>
  </div>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${email}?subject=${subject}&body=${body}`}>{email}</a> from the email address you use to sign in to Wallyt, with the subject “Delete my Wallyt
      account”.
    </li>
    <li>
      We reply to confirm. If you write from a different address, we’ll send a code to your Wallyt
      address to check the account is yours.
    </li>
    <li>We delete your account within 30 days, and email you when it’s done.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>If you own a group</strong> that other people have joined, you can make someone else
      the owner first, from the group’s settings. Otherwise ownership passes to its longest-standing
      admin, or to its longest-standing member if it has no admins.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What we delete</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your account: your email address, name and photo.</li>
    <li>Your Google or Apple sign-in link, and every signed-in session.</li>
    <li>Your email address, phone number and photo from each group you were in.</li>
    <li>
      Groups nobody else has joined, with all their expenses and history. People you added who
      never joined don’t count, since they can’t open the group.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What stays with your groups</h2>
  <p>
    Expenses are shared records: the other people in a group rely on them for their own balances.
    So expenses and payments you were part of, and their history, stay in those groups. They
    show the name you had in that group, but nothing else about you, and they’re no longer
    connected to an account: where they said you added or changed something, they now say
    “Someone”. The other people in the group can still edit or delete them.
  </p>

  <h2>How long it takes</h2>
  <p>
    In the app, your account is deleted straight away. By email, it is deleted within 30 days of
    your request. If any copy of it remains in a backup, it is erased within 30 days after that.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting some data without closing your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Remove or change your photo and name in Wallyt, from Account, or for one group from your own row
      in its settings.
    </li>
    <li>Leave a group from its settings. Its past expenses keep your name, as described above.</li>
    <li>
      To have something else removed, such as a photo someone added of you or an expense, email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> and tell us what it is.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Read the full <a href={url('/wallyt/privacy')}>Wallyt privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</Doc>

<style>
  .request {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px 18px;
    margin: 1.6em 0 0;
  }

  .request p {
    flex: 1 1 18em;
    margin: 0 !important;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted) !important;
  }

  .request .button {
    color: var(--bg);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
</style>
